---
// GroundTexture.astro — the drafting-paper grid (DESIGN-ELEVATION.md §1.3(c),
// §3.1): a 32px hairline grid at ~3.5% white, the one aesthetic risk this
// phase takes on. Rendered only by Section.astro's `texture` prop, which has
// exactly two call sites — the hero and the closing CTA — so the grid
// bookends the page rather than wallpapering it (spending it everywhere
// would make it decoration instead of material).
//
// Static paint only: CLAUDE.md's "transforms and opacity only" rule means a
// background-image is never animated, so this component ships no script and
// needs no motion-safe branch — there is nothing to suppress under reduced
// motion or JS-disabled.
---

<div aria-hidden="true" class="ground-texture absolute inset-0 bg-grid-draft">
</div>

<style>
  /* Block-axis fade so the grid dissolves at the band's own edges rather
   * than hard-cutting (§3.1). Vertical only — no RTL variant needed (§5.2:
   * "a repeating pattern has no inherent inline direction; it tiles
   * identically either way"). */
  .ground-texture {
    mask-image: linear-gradient(
      to bottom,
      transparent 0%,
      black 12%,
      black 88%,
      transparent 100%
    );
    -webkit-mask-image: linear-gradient(
      to bottom,
      transparent 0%,
      black 12%,
      black 88%,
      transparent 100%
    );
  }
</style>
